# Switches for warband_nx, read at startup from
# sdmc:/switch/warband/args.txt
#
# hbmenu launches an .nro with no arguments, and every diagnostic in this
# build is a command-line switch - so this file is the only way to turn one on
# without rebuilding. One per line or all on one line; blank lines and
# anything after a # are ignored. Everything here is commented out, so as it
# stands this file changes nothing.
#
# --seconds=N          stop after N seconds (default: run until closed)
# --svcs=N             stop after N import calls; 0 is no cap, and 0 is the
#                      default on this platform. A small number is how you
#                      bisect a hang: run to N, read the histogram.
# --ticks=N            guest instructions per Run() before coming back
# --threads=N          cap on guest threads
# --shot=PATH          write PATH_01.bmp, PATH_02.bmp ... from the back buffer,
#                      e.g. --shot=sdmc:/switch/warband/shot
# --shot-every=N       seconds between those grabs
# --gl-errors          ask the driver after every GL call whether it objected
# --gl-trace           name every GL call before it is made (very slow)
# --log-calls=SEC      name every import the engine makes, from SEC onwards
# --trace              sample the guest pc and symbolise it
# --trace-from=SEC     start sampling that many seconds in
# --no-draw            keep every GL call except the draws
# --overlay            frame counter on. Off here by default: its shader
#                      has no precision qualifier and GLES will not
#                      compile it, so it draws nothing and complains.
# --no-overlay         no frame counter
# --rec=PATH.wav       write everything the mixer produced
# --check-verts        describe the box each draw's positions cover
# --no-draw-guard      leave out-of-range vertex arrays enabled
